{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 never sets recv_buf_valid, causing `TRAP: uart timeout, no byte received` and `FAIL 0xdead` instead of a received byte. Expected recv_divcnt to count up to cfg_divider (64) to leave recv_state 1, but it stays 0. Root cause in excerpt line 74 `recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 0` never increments, so `2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider` never fires and receiver stalls.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@
 			recv_buf_data <= 0;
 			recv_buf_valid <= 0;
 		end else begin
-			recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 0;
+			recv_divcnt <= recv_divcnt + 1;
 			if (reg_dat_re)
 				recv_buf_valid <= 0;
 			case (recv_state)", "expected": "tohost PASS (no TRAP: uart timeout), loopback byte 0xa5 received with divider 64"}

